Z||000010||onfire||09-20-2001||04:53 AM||||On a side note did you know that?<P>A Seattle architect named Minoru Yamasaki designed the World Trade Center.He worked for the architect firm Skilling, Ward, Magnusson, and Barkshire, which drew up the plans for the WTC. He was commissioned to design it in 1963. Groundbreaking was in 1966. The ribbon cutting for the opening was in 1973, with other aspects of the project not complete til 1977. Minoru Yamasaki died in 1987.<P>Pacific Car & Foundry Co. at the time (1967) a Seattle company fabricated the steel used to erect the twin 110-story towers. They shut down the structual steel division in 1973. They are now known as Paccar.<P>The planes used in the attack were made by another Seattle company. The Boeing Co. has since moved its headquarters to Chicago.<P>The source for this info. came from the Seattle P.I.<p>[This message has been edited by onfire (edited 09-20-2001).]||||reg||1
